<!--
  SecretPrinter.Proxy.csproj

  Written by Claude (Anthropic model, Claude Opus 4.5) at the direction of
  Edwin West, for the SecretPrinter project.

  The paragraph about reviewing this project's files corrected by Claude
  (Anthropic model, Claude Opus 5) at the direction of Edwin West, 2026-09-15,
  when CertificatePin.cs was added. Reviewed by a human before merge.

  InternalsVisibleTo added by Claude (Anthropic model, Claude Opus 5) at the
  direction of Edwin West, 2026-09-21. Reviewed by a human before merge.

  The print path: moves job bytes between a client and the printer.

  This project contains NOTHING else, on purpose. It is where the two claims the
  README leads with must be checkable:

    REQ-PXY-003  the payload is never inspected or modified
    REQ-PXY-004  the payload is never written to disk

  A reviewer answers "does this ever touch my documents?" by reading this
  project's few source files, not the whole solution. A test in
  SecretPrinter.Proxy.Tests reads this assembly's own metadata and fails if it
  references any file-writing type.

  There were two source files until 2026-09-15. The third, CertificatePin.cs,
  decides whether the printer is the one whose certificate fingerprint was
  pinned. It belongs here rather than in a project of its own because the
  encrypted connection to the printer carries the job bytes: anyone reviewing
  the print path has to read how the printer at the other end is verified.

  It knows nothing about mDNS, discovery or printers: it is handed a delegate
  that returns where to connect, and that is all it knows about the world.

  Internals are visible to SecretPrinter.Proxy.Tests, and to nothing else. The
  one internal member that needs it is TcpConnectionFactory's second
  constructor, which replaces only the socket connect so the connect deadline
  can be tested without a network. It was added with the fix for
  docs/findings/2026-09-17-connect-timeout-is-not-reported.md. It changes
  nothing the service can do: the service uses the public constructor.

  Common build settings come from Directory.Build.props at the repository root.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>SecretPrinter.Proxy</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>SecretPrinter.Proxy</AssemblyName>
    <Description>Streams IPP print jobs between a client and the printer.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../SecretPrinter.Spec/SecretPrinter.Spec.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="SecretPrinter.Proxy.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
